from common import U,Q,S,T
UNITS=[
U("B101","Hasil, durasi, dan hubungan ke sekarang","Memilih Perfect Simple atau Continuous berdasarkan fokus.",
"Have been + ing|For since|How long|Hasil jumlah|Proses durasi|Stative verbs",
"Present Perfect Simple sering menyoroti hasil atau jumlah yang selesai: I've written three emails. Present Perfect Continuous sering menyoroti proses atau lamanya kegiatan sampai sekarang: I've been writing emails for an hour. Keduanya dapat benar dengan fokus berbeda; jumlah tiga email lebih cocok dengan hasil yang dihitung.||For menyebut durasi; since menyebut titik awal. I have known her for years memakai simple karena know dalam makna ini stative. Continuous tidak otomatis berarti kegiatan masih berlangsung saat berbicara: I've been running dapat menjelaskan mengapa pembicara sekarang berkeringat setelah berhenti.",
[("have/has + V3 + jumlah","She has read three chapters.","Hasil terhitung."),("have/has been + V-ing","She has been reading for an hour.","Durasi/proses."),("since + titik; for + durasi","since Monday; for three days","Awal versus panjang waktu.")],
("I have been knowing her since 2020.","I have known her since 2020.","Know dalam makna mengenal biasanya stative."),
"Rafi has been working on the club newsletter since Monday. He has written two articles, but the third is unfinished. Ana has known him for five years. She has been checking the layout this morning and is taking a break now.",
"newsletter=buletin|layout=tata letak|unfinished=belum selesai|duration=durasi|result=hasil|take a break=beristirahat",
[Q("Fokus jumlah selesai: She ___ three reports.","has written","has been writing three completed reports||is write","Perfect Simple cocok untuk hasil yang dihitung."),
Q("I have lived here ___ 2021.","since","for||during five","Since memperkenalkan titik awal."),
Q("I have been studying ___ two hours.","for","since||at","For memperkenalkan durasi."),
Q("I've been running dapat menjelaskan …","keadaan lelah sekarang setelah kegiatan","bahwa kegiatan pasti belum berhenti||bahwa kegiatan terjadi tahun lalu saja","Continuous dapat menjelaskan akibat proses yang baru berhenti.","meaning"),
Q("Berapa artikel Rafi yang belum selesai?","one","two||all three","Dua selesai, artikel ketiga belum.","reading"),
S("Perbaiki: She has been knowing Ana for years.","She has known Ana for years.","Know dalam makna ini memakai perfect simple.")],
[T("speaking","Laporkan proyek rekaan: hasil terhitung, proses yang memakan waktu, dan hambatan.","I've written two sections. I've been checking the figures since Monday. I haven't finished the conclusion because one result is missing.","Hasil dan proses dibedakan|For/since tepat|Hambatan dijelaskan"),
T("writing","Tulis pembaruan proyek lima kalimat, memakai dua perfect simple dan satu perfect continuous.","We have finished two posters. We have collected ten books. Ana has been checking the list since Monday. One title is still missing. We will ask the librarian tomorrow.","Jumlah selesai jelas|Durasi masuk akal|Rencana tindak lanjut")],"perfect",("A208",)),
U("B102","Urutan masa lalu yang lebih dalam","Menata narasi dengan Past Simple, Continuous, dan Perfect.",
"Had + V3|Earlier past|Latar continuous|By the time|Before after|Tidak overuse perfect",
"Past Perfect menunjukkan kejadian yang lebih dahulu daripada titik lampau lain: When I arrived, the meeting had started. Acuan arrived penting; had started tidak sekadar berarti 'sudah' tanpa hubungan waktu. Past Simple melanjutkan kejadian utama, dan Past Continuous memberi latar berlangsung.||Jika before atau after sudah menjelaskan urutan, Past Simple kadang cukup. Gunakan Past Perfect saat hubungan waktu perlu diperjelas atau penulis ingin menyoroti kejadian lebih awal. Setelah urutan terbentuk, jangan menulis seluruh cerita dengan had; pembaca membutuhkan garis waktu utama yang jelas.",
[("earlier event: had + V3","The bus had left when we arrived.","Bus pergi lebih dulu."),("background: was/were + V-ing","People were waiting outside.","Latar."),("main event: V2","We called the organiser.","Kejadian utama berikutnya.")],
("When I arrived, the bus has left.","When I arrived, the bus had left.","Titik acuan lampau memerlukan had untuk kejadian lebih dulu."),
"When Ana reached the station, the train had already left. She had misread the departure time. Rain was falling, and several passengers were waiting inside. Ana called Rafi, bought another ticket, and arrived an hour later.",
"departure=keberangkatan|misread=salah membaca|reach=tiba di|passenger=penumpang|already=lebih dahulu|by the time=pada saat",
[Q("The train had left when Ana arrived. Yang terjadi lebih dulu …","the train left","Ana arrived||keduanya pasti bersamaan","Past Perfect menempatkan keberangkatan lebih awal.","meaning"),
Q("She ___ the wrong time before she left home.","had written","has written||is writing","Titik acuan lampau memakai had + V3."),
Q("Latar yang sedang berlangsung dalam bacaan …","Rain was falling.","Ana bought a ticket.||The train had left.","Continuous memberi latar berlangsung.","reading"),
Q("Mengapa Ana terlambat?","She had misread the departure time.","Rafi hid her ticket.||There were no trains all day.","Bacaan menyebut kesalahan membaca jadwal.","reading"),
Q("Setelah latar dibentuk, rangkaian utama paling wajar …","She called Rafi and bought a ticket.","She had called and had bought forever.||She has call and buy.","Past Simple melanjutkan kejadian utama."),
S("Lengkapi: By the time we arrived, the film ___ started.","had","Film mulai sebelum titik arrived.")],
[T("speaking","Ceritakan kesalahpahaman jadwal dengan tiga lapis waktu: sebab lebih awal, latar, kejadian utama.","I had written the wrong time. People were leaving when I arrived. I called the organiser and joined the next session.","Urutan logis|Had + V3|Narasi utama simple past"),
T("writing","Tulis cerita 80–100 kata tentang barang tertinggal dan solusi; tandai satu Past Perfect.","Yesterday, I arrived at the library to give a short presentation. Other students were preparing their notes when I opened my bag. I realised that I had left my notebook at home. At first, I felt worried because the talk was due to start in ten minutes. Then I remembered that I had a copy on my phone. I asked the librarian to print it and checked the pages carefully. The presentation started on time, and I thanked her afterwards.","80–100 kata|Tiga lapis waktu|Solusi berhubungan dengan masalah")],"past",("B101",)),
U("B103","Rencana dengan syarat dan tenggat","Menyatakan masa depan dalam jadwal, janji, dan klausa waktu.",
"Will going to review|When before after until|Present in time clauses|Future Continuous|Deadlines|Clarifying plans",
"Sesudah when, after, before, atau as soon as yang berfungsi sebagai klausa waktu masa depan, gunakan bentuk present: I'll call when I arrive. Ini berbeda dari pertanyaan tak langsung I don't know when she will arrive, yang menanyakan waktu kedatangan, bukan menjadi syarat waktu tindakan lain.||Future Continuous memakai will be + V-ing untuk kegiatan yang diperkirakan berlangsung pada titik masa depan: At ten, I'll be travelling. Pelajari tenggat dengan by, yang berarti selambat-lambatnya; until menyatakan keberlangsungan sampai suatu batas. Pemilihan preposisi dapat mengubah janji kerja.",
[("will + V1 + when + present","I'll send it when I finish.","Klausa waktu."),("will be + V-ing","At nine, I'll be presenting.","Proses di titik masa depan."),("by ≠ until","Submit by Friday; work until Friday.","Tenggat versus durasi.")],
("I'll call you when I will arrive.","I'll call you when I arrive.","Klausa waktu masa depan memakai present."),
"The club will open at nine on Saturday. At ten, Ana will be showing visitors around. Rafi will email the final map when he finishes it. Volunteers must send their names by Thursday. The desk will stay open until five.",
"deadline=tenggat|volunteer=relawan|as soon as=segera setelah|until=sampai selama proses|by=selambat-lambatnya|show around=memandu berkeliling",
[Q("I'll email you when I ___ the report.","finish","will finish||finished yesterday","When membentuk klausa waktu masa depan."),
Q("At ten tomorrow, I ___ to Bandung.","will be travelling","will travelling||will be travel","Future Continuous = will be + ing."),
Q("Send it by Friday berarti …","kirim selambat-lambatnya Jumat","kirim terus-menerus sampai Jumat||kirim hanya setelah Jumat","By menyatakan tenggat.","meaning"),
Q("Stay here until five berarti …","tetap di sini sampai pukul lima","datang pertama kali setelah lima||pergi paling lambat sebelum satu","Until menyatakan keberlangsungan.","meaning"),
Q("Apa yang Ana lakukan pukul sepuluh?","showing visitors around","closing the desk||sending volunteer names","Bacaan menyebut kegiatan itu secara eksplisit.","reading"),
S("Lengkapi: I'll start as soon as she ___. (arrive)","arrives","Klausa waktu memakai present; she mendapat s.")],
[T("speaking","Susun rencana acara dengan satu tenggat, satu kegiatan berlangsung, dan satu klausa waktu.","Send your names by Thursday. At ten, we'll be welcoming guests. We'll open the room when the guide arrives.","By/until dibedakan|Future Continuous tepat|Present sesudah when"),
T("writing","Buat pesan pembagian tugas enam kalimat dengan jadwal dan tenggat jelas.","Please send your names by Thursday. We will check the list on Friday. On Saturday, the desk will open at nine. At ten, Ana will be welcoming guests. Rafi will send the map when he finishes it. The desk will stay open until five.","Tenggat eksplisit|Pembagian tugas jelas|Pola masa depan sesuai fungsi")],"future",("B102",)),
U("B104","Sebab, kemungkinan, dan pengandaian","Membedakan kondisi umum, kemungkinan nyata, dan situasi hipotetis.",
"Zero conditional|First conditional|Second conditional|Unless|Could would|Makna sebelum rumus",
"Zero conditional menyatakan hubungan umum: If ice gets warm enough, it melts. First conditional membicarakan kemungkinan masa depan yang dianggap nyata: If it rains, we'll move inside. Second conditional membayangkan keadaan kini/masa depan yang lebih jauh dari kenyataan: If I had more time, I would join.||Bentuk lampau pada second conditional tidak selalu berarti masa lalu; ia dapat menunjukkan jarak hipotetis. Unless berarti if not dalam banyak penggunaan, tetapi jangan mengganti secara buta ketika makna berubah. Will bukan satu-satunya hasil first conditional; can, may, atau instruksi dapat dipakai sesuai maksud.",
[("if + present, present","If water freezes, it expands.","Hubungan umum."),("if + present, will + V1","If it rains, we'll stay inside.","Kemungkinan nyata."),("if + past, would + V1","If I had time, I'd join.","Hipotetis kini/masa depan.")],
("If I will have time, I will join. (kondisi biasa)","If I have time, I will join.","Klausa if kondisi masa depan biasa memakai present."),
"Ana may join a weekend course if her work finishes early. Rafi cannot afford the fee now. He says, 'If I had more money, I would join too.' The organiser says the outdoor activity will continue unless it rains.",
"afford=mampu membayar|fee=biaya|unless=kecuali jika/jika tidak|condition=syarat|possible=mungkin|hypothetical=andaian",
[Q("If she ___ early, we'll start at nine.","arrives","will arrives||would arrive","First conditional memakai present pada if."),
Q("If I had more time, I would read more menunjuk …","andaian sekarang/masa depan","kejadian pasti kemarin||perintah membaca","Past form menandai jarak hipotetis.","meaning"),
Q("We'll go unless it rains berarti …","kami pergi jika tidak hujan","kami hanya pergi saat hujan||kami pasti pergi meski hujan","Unless di sini setara if not.","meaning"),
Q("If water freezes, it expands termasuk …","hubungan umum","janji khusus besok||penyesalan lampau","Zero conditional menggambarkan hubungan umum."),
Q("Mengapa Rafi belum dapat mengikuti kursus?","He cannot afford the fee.","He dislikes weekends.||He has already finished it.","Kendala keuangan dinyatakan dalam bacaan.","reading"),
S("Lengkapi: If I had a bicycle, I ___ cycle to school.","would","Would + V1 menyatakan hasil hipotetis.")],
[T("speaking","Usulkan rencana acara: kondisi normal, rencana jika hujan, dan satu ide andaikan dana cukup.","We meet outside if the weather is fine. If it rains, we'll use the hall. If we had more money, we would invite a musician.","First/second bermakna|Rencana alternatif jelas|Kondisi realistis dibedakan dari andaian"),
T("writing","Tulis empat aturan keputusan untuk memilih kegiatan klub, memakai if dan unless.","If we have ten members, we'll book a room. We'll meet outside unless it rains. If the room is busy, we can use the library. If we had more time, we would organise a larger event.","Empat keputusan|Unless tepat|Could/can/would sesuai makna")],"conditionals",("B103",)),
U("B105","Mengubah fokus dengan Passive Voice","Mengutamakan proses atau objek ketika pelaku bukan fokus.",
"Be + V3|Active passive|Agent by|Present passive|Past passive|Transitive verbs",
"Passive memindahkan fokus ke pihak yang menerima tindakan: The librarian checks the books → The books are checked by the librarian. Tense ditandai pada be; kata kerja utama menjadi V3. Pelaku boleh dihilangkan bila tidak diketahui, sudah jelas, atau tidak relevan.||Tidak semua kata kerja bisa dipasifkan. Kata kerja seperti arrive tidak memiliki objek yang dapat menjadi subjek passive. Untuk prosedur, passive membantu fokus pada langkah: The form is checked; the card is printed. Jangan memilih passive hanya agar kalimat terlihat lebih formal; pilih berdasarkan informasi yang perlu ditonjolkan.",
[("S + am/is/are + V3","The books are checked daily.","Proses sekarang."),("S + was/were + V3","The room was cleaned yesterday.","Peristiwa lampau."),("by + pelaku","The poster was designed by Ana.","Pelaku relevan.")],
("The books are check every day.","The books are checked every day.","Passive membutuhkan V3 setelah be."),
"At the community library, returned books are checked at the front desk. Damaged books are repaired before they are placed on the shelves. Last week, a new reading corner was opened by local volunteers. Visitors can use it without a fee.",
"return=mengembalikan|damaged=rusak|repair=memperbaiki|shelf=rak|process=proses|volunteer=relawan",
[Q("The room ___ yesterday.","was cleaned","is clean by yesterday||was clean","Lampau passive = was + V3."),
Q("The books ___ every day.","are checked","is checked||are checking by","Subjek jamak memakai are + V3."),
Q("Kalimat yang tidak cocok dipasifkan dengan pola objek biasa …","The train arrived.","Ana repaired the chair.||Rafi wrote the report.","Arrive tidak memiliki objek."),
Q("Alasan menghilangkan by the staff pada prosedur …","pelakunya sudah jelas atau bukan fokus","semua passive harus tanpa pelaku||pelaku tidak pernah penting","Pemilihan bergantung fokus informasi.","meaning"),
Q("Apa yang terjadi sebelum buku rusak dikembalikan ke rak?","They are repaired.","They are sold.||They are thrown away.","Before memberi urutan proses.","reading"),
S("Ubah ke passive: Ana wrote the report.","The report was written by Ana.","Objek menjadi subjek; wrote menjadi was written.")],
[T("speaking","Jelaskan proses peminjaman buku dalam empat langkah passive.","The card is checked. The book is scanned. The return date is printed. The book is given to the reader.","Urutan jelas|Be + V3|Fokus proses"),
T("writing","Tulis pengumuman tiga perbaikan yang selesai minggu lalu, lalu satu informasi pelaku yang relevan.","The chairs were repaired last week. The walls were painted. A new shelf was installed. The mural was designed by local students.","Past passive|Agreement tepat|By digunakan saat informatif")],"passive",("B104",)),
U("B106","Menambah informasi dengan Relative Clauses","Menghubungkan orang, benda, dan tempat tanpa rujukan kabur.",
"Who which that|Where|Defining clauses|Subject object relatives|Omission dasar|Rujukan jelas",
"Relative clause memberi informasi tentang noun sebelumnya: the student who won the prize; the book that I borrowed. Who lazim untuk orang, which untuk benda, dan that bisa menggantikan keduanya pada banyak defining clauses. Where menghubungkan tempat dengan kegiatan di dalamnya.||Dalam the book that I borrowed, that adalah objek dan dapat dihilangkan: the book I borrowed. Dalam the student who won, who adalah subjek dan tidak boleh dihapus dengan cara yang sama. Hindari mengulang objek menjadi the book that I borrowed it. Informasi defining membantu menentukan orang/benda mana yang dimaksud.",
[("noun + who + verb","the teacher who helped us","Who adalah subjek."),("noun + that + S + verb","the book that I borrowed","That adalah objek."),("place + where + clause","the library where we study","Hubungan tempat.")],
("The book that I bought it is useful.","The book that I bought is useful.","It mengulang objek yang sudah diwakili that."),
"Our club needs a volunteer who can design posters. We also need a room where ten people can study. Ana knows a teacher who works at the library. The teacher recommended a website that offers free drawing lessons.",
"volunteer=relawan|recommend=merekomendasikan|offer=menawarkan|design=merancang|relative clause=klausa penerang|prize=hadiah",
[Q("The person ___ helped me is Ana.","who","where||what","Who merujuk orang sebagai subjek."),
Q("The room ___ we meet is quiet.","where","who||what","Where menghubungkan tempat."),
Q("Klausa yang boleh menghilangkan relative pronoun …","the book that I bought","the person who called||the bus that stopped","That adalah objek dalam I bought [it]."),
Q("Pilih revisi tepat.","The film that I watched was interesting.","The film that I watched it was interesting.||The film who I watched was interesting.","Hindari objek ganda it."),
Q("Keahlian relawan yang dibutuhkan …","designing posters","repairing trains||selling tickets","Bacaan menyebut design posters.","reading"),
S("Gabungkan: I know a teacher. She works here. Mulai dengan I know.","I know a teacher who works here.||I know a teacher that works here.","Who/that menghubungkan orang dan tindakan.")],
[T("speaking","Jelaskan tiga orang/benda tanpa menyebut namanya agar pendamping menebak.","It's a person who helps readers. It's a place where we borrow books. It's a thing that we use to draw straight lines.","Relative clauses tepat|Petunjuk cukup|Tidak mengulang objek"),
T("writing","Buat iklan kebutuhan klub lima kalimat dengan who, where, dan that.","We need a volunteer who can draw. We need a room where ten people can sit. We also need a printer that works well. Ana knows a teacher who can help. Please contact our club on Friday.","Tiga jenis rujukan|Defining information jelas|Pesan dapat ditindaklanjuti")],"clauses",("B105",)),
U("B107","Melaporkan ucapan dan pertanyaan","Menyampaikan pesan orang lain dengan perubahan rujukan yang tepat.",
"Said told|Backshift dasar|Pronoun time changes|Reported questions|If whether|No inversion",
"Reported speech menyampaikan isi ucapan, bukan mengutip kata demi kata. Ana said, 'I am tired' dapat menjadi Ana said she was tired. Told memerlukan orang yang diberi tahu: She told me; said tidak langsung memakai me dengan pola yang sama.||Backshift sering muncul setelah reporting verb lampau, tetapi tidak selalu wajib jika informasi masih berlaku. Kata ganti serta here/today/tomorrow berubah sesuai lokasi dan waktu pelaporan, bukan secara otomatis. Reported questions memakai urutan pernyataan: She asked where I lived, bukan where did I live. Yes/no question dilaporkan dengan if atau whether.",
[("said + clause","She said she was busy.","Melaporkan pernyataan."),("told + orang + clause","She told me she was busy.","Ada penerima pesan."),("asked + if/wh + S + V","He asked where I lived.","Urutan pernyataan.")],
("She asked where did I live.","She asked where I lived.","Pertanyaan tak langsung tidak memakai inversi do/did."),
"On Monday, Ana said, 'I am preparing the posters.' She told Rafi that she needed two more photos. Rafi asked whether the library could print them. On Tuesday, he reported that Ana had been preparing the posters the day before.",
"report=melaporkan|quote=kutipan|whether=apakah|the day before=sehari sebelumnya|prepare=menyiapkan|message=pesan",
[Q("She ___ me she was ready.","told","said||spoke that","Told diikuti penerima pesan."),
Q("Reported question yang tepat …","He asked where I worked.","He asked where did I work.||He asked where worked I.","Urutan pernyataan dipertahankan."),
Q("Yes/no question dapat dilaporkan dengan …","if or whether","because only||whose always","If/whether memperkenalkan pertanyaan ya/tidak."),
Q("Perubahan tomorrow dalam pelaporan bergantung pada …","waktu pelaporan","jumlah huruf kalimat||jenis kelamin pembicara","Penyesuaian mengikuti konteks rujukan.","meaning"),
Q("Berapa foto tambahan yang dibutuhkan Ana?","two","one||three","Isi pesan menyebut two more photos.","reading"),
S("Lengkapi: She asked ___ I was ready. (pakai whether)","whether","Whether memperkenalkan pertanyaan ya/tidak.")],
[T("speaking","Dengarkan tiga pesan rekaan dari pendamping dan laporkan kepada orang ketiga tanpa mengubah maksud.","Ana said she needed two photos. Rafi asked whether the printer worked. Lina told me the room was ready.","Isi akurat|Said/told tepat|Pertanyaan tanpa inversi"),
T("writing","Ubah tiga catatan dialog menjadi ringkasan: Ana: I need paper. Rafi: Is the room open? Lina: We can meet tomorrow. Pelaporan dilakukan hari yang sama.","Ana said she needed paper. Rafi asked whether the room was open. Lina said they could meet tomorrow.","Rujukan waktu sesuai konteks|Tiga pesan terjaga|Reported question tepat")],"reported",("B106",)),
U("B108","Pendapat dengan alasan dan contoh","Menulis paragraf dan email yang memiliki tujuan serta dukungan.",
"Topic sentence|Reason evidence example|However therefore|Polite email|Request clarification|Revision",
"Paragraf pendapat yang kuat menyatakan satu gagasan, memberi alasan, lalu menunjukkan contoh atau bukti yang relevan. Contoh bukan bukti bahwa sesuatu selalu benar. Pisahkan pengalaman pribadi dari klaim umum. However memberi kontras; therefore menyatakan kesimpulan yang harus benar-benar mengikuti alasan sebelumnya.||Email permintaan dimulai dengan tujuan, disusul konteks yang diperlukan, pertanyaan spesifik, dan penutup. Gunakan bahasa sopan tanpa membuat kalimat berputar-putar. Saat merevisi, periksa hubungan logis antarkalimat, rujukan pronoun, tense, dan apakah penerima tahu tindakan yang diminta.",
[("claim → reason → example → implication","The club needs longer sessions because members need time to practise.","Bangun dukungan."),("Could you + V1 …?","Could you confirm the room's capacity?","Permintaan sopan.")],
("The room is small. Therefore, the tickets are blue.","The room is small. Therefore, we can invite only ten people.","Therefore membutuhkan hubungan kesimpulan yang logis."),
"Our club should meet for ninety minutes. Members currently spend most of the hour reviewing vocabulary, so they have little time for speaking. A longer session would allow a short discussion after the review. However, we should ask members about their schedules before changing the timetable.",
"claim=pernyataan yang diajukan|evidence=bukti|confirm=memastikan|capacity=kapasitas|however=namun|therefore=oleh karena itu",
[Q("Fungsi kalimat pertama bacaan …","menyatakan usulan utama","mengutip hasil eksperimen||memberi salam penutup","Itu posisi utama yang dikembangkan.","reading"),
Q("Dukungan utama usulan sesi lebih panjang …","waktu berbicara saat ini terlalu sedikit","ruangannya selalu kosong||semua anggota sudah setuju","Alasan berasal dari alokasi waktu.","reading"),
Q("However pada bacaan memperkenalkan …","pertimbangan pembatas","kesimpulan pasti||contoh pengucapan","Jadwal anggota perlu diperiksa dahulu.","discourse"),
Q("Permintaan email yang paling spesifik …","Could you confirm whether the room seats twenty people?","Tell me everything soon.||Room good?","Pertanyaan spesifik mudah dijawab.","writing"),
Q("Kalimat kesimpulan yang didukung 'room seats ten' …","We should limit this session to ten participants.","Everyone will enjoy the session.||The session will certainly be free.","Kapasitas mendukung batas peserta, bukan klaim lain.","reasoning"),
S("Lengkapi: ___ you confirm the time, please? (permintaan sopan memakai could)","Could","Could + subjek + V1 membentuk permintaan.")],
[T("speaking","Berikan usulan kegiatan 90 detik: pendapat, dua alasan, contoh, dan satu keterbatasan.","I suggest a longer reading session. We need time to discuss books, and new members need support. Last week, two people could not finish. However, we should check everyone's schedule first.","Argumen didukung|Ada keterbatasan|Penyampaian runtut"),
T("writing","Tulis email 100–130 kata kepada pengelola ruang. Jelaskan kegiatan, kapasitas, jadwal, dan dua pertanyaan.","Dear Library Team, I am writing to ask about booking a room for our English club. We plan to meet on Saturday afternoon for ninety minutes. There will be about fifteen members, and we would like to practise speaking in small groups. Our usual room is too small, so we are looking for a quieter space. Could you confirm whether your meeting room can seat fifteen people? We would also like to know whether there is a charge for community groups. If the room is available, please let us know how to make a reservation and what equipment is included. Thank you for your help. Best regards, Ana","100–130 kata|Dua permintaan spesifik|Register sopan dan jelas")],"paragraph",("B107",))
]
